    "turn_text": "I actually like Johnson's approach better and his approach right now is to aggressively pass the remaining appropriation bills in an expedited timeline. So for example, last week we passed, as soon as he was elected, we passed the Israel resolution and then we passed the energy and water bills. This week, we are scheduled to pass the legislative branch appropriation bill and then the Department of Interior and Environment bill and then the housing and urban development bill all in one day. three appropriation bills in one day that will put us to the point where we passed eight of the 12 with time with still time to pass the remaining four. So it's an aggressive timeline. I think we can get it done. It's going to be a very late Thursday. It's going to be a very, very long Thursday. But I'm excited. I think it's the right path. And the other thing, if you want to get an indication of of Mike Johnson's fiscal worldview. He's shaking DC already because the aid package to Israel that everyone is supporting. He is supporting, and he's not going to trade it for Ukraine. And he's saying that the aid has to be paid for out of cuts from the appropriations. So the federal government can't print money, can't go to debt, to support Israel. If we're going to do it, we're going to make a sacrifice. And I think that that it is shaking Washington, DC. And so I'm excited about that.",
